#### Article 19

1. Prevention of Violence Against Women as referred to in Article 18 letter a may be carried out in the following forms:
a. developing media for communication, information, education and public campaigns;
b. developing educational materials and curricula;
c. developing safe transportation systems and public spaces;
d. establishing early detection systems, security and integrated complaint services in industrial areas, companies, residential areas, educational environments, Islamic boarding schools and other public spaces;
e. providing consultation, information, education, and counseling services;
f. developing policies related to safe and friendly schools/madrasahs, boarding schools, Islamic boarding schools, and higher education institutions;
g. forming and developing cadres, communities, and groups from among youth, students, Islamic students, university students, journalists, social media influencers, educators, and religious leaders;
h. conducting education and advocacy to owners, managers and/or users of social media;
i. developing protection systems and special support for vulnerable women groups;
j. conducting awareness-raising for perpetrators;
k. increasing the capacity of regional governments, government agencies, institutions, community institutions, business sector, Islamic boarding schools, community organizations, media, religious leaders, community leaders and communities;
l. conducting cooperation with religious institutions, community social institutions, service institutions, higher education institutions, Islamic boarding schools, media, youth organizations, religious leaders and community leaders; and
m. conducting socialization of laws and regulations.
2. Forms of prevention of Violence Against Women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

## Part Three

Services for Women Victims of Violence

#### Article 20

Women victims of violence receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity respected as human beings;
b. the right to recovery;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain easy access to information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling that is fast, appropriate, comfortable and according to needs;
h. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilities in the judicial process;
i. the right to assistance; and
j. the right to a sense of security.

#### Article 21

Services for women victims of violence may be carried out through:
a. receiving reports and/or outreach to victims of violence;
b. providing information about the rights of victims of violence;
c. facilitating the provision of health services;
d. facilitating the provision of psychological strengthening services;
e. facilitating the provision of psychosocial services, social rehabilitation, social empowerment, repatriation, and social reintegration;
f. providing legal services;
g. identifying economic empowerment needs;
h. identifying temporary shelter needs for victims of violence and families of victims of violence that need to be fulfilled immediately;
i. facilitating the needs of victims of violence with disabilities;
j. coordinating and cooperating on the fulfillment of the rights of victims of violence with other institutions; and
k. monitoring the fulfillment of the rights of victims of violence by law enforcement officials during the judicial process.

## Part Four

Strengthening Institutional Protection for Women

#### Article 22

1. Strengthening institutional Protection for Women may be carried out through capacity building, cooperation and integration with:
a. government agencies;
b. educational institutions;
c. religious institutions;
d. health service provider institutions;
e. professional institutions;
f. business sector;
g. service institutions;
h. Islamic boarding schools;
i. youth organizations;
j. legal aid organizations;
k. media;
l. religious leaders;
m. community leaders;
n. communities; and
o. families.
2. Strengthening and developing institutions providing Protection for Women services shall be implemented through:
a. capacity building of human resources of institutions providing Protection for Women victims of violence services at the Regional level;
b. provision of specific needs for women in emergency situations and special conditions at the Regional level;
c. development of communication, information, and education strategies regarding the protection of women's rights at the Regional level;
d. strengthening networks among institutions providing Protection for Women services at the Regional level;
e. facilitating efforts to fulfill standards of institutions providing Protection for Women services at the Regional level;
f. developing institutions providing Protection for Women services at the Regional level.

# CHAPTER VI

## STRATEGY FOR EMPOWERMENT AND PROTECTION OF WOMEN

#### Article 23

1. Empowerment and Protection of Women shall be implemented by integrating gender mainstreaming and gender-disaggregated data based on laws and regulations.
2. Empowerment and Protection of Women shall be implemented with working groups and/or integrated services established by Mayor's Decree.
3. Empowerment and Protection of Women shall be coordinated by the Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of Empowerment and Protection of Women.

# CHAPTER VII

MECHANISM FOR IMPLEMENTING EMPOWERMENT AND PROTECTION OF WOMEN

## Part One

General

#### Article 24

The mechanism for implementing Empowerment and Protection of Women shall be carried out through the following stages:
a. formulation of policy planning for programs and activities;
b. budgeting of programs and activities;
c. implementation of programs and activities; and
d. monitoring, evaluation and reporting.

## Part Two

Formulation of Policy Planning for Programs and Activities

#### Article 25

1. Formulation of policy planning for programs and activities as referred to in Article 24 letter a, shall be implemented through:
a. mapping, collection, processing and presentation of data;
b. coordination and synchronization of planning for programs and activities with related Regional Apparatus; and
c. determination of programs and activities in planning documents.
2. Formulation of policy planning for programs and activities shall be implemented based on minimum service standards and standard operating procedures.
3. Formulation of policy planning for programs and activities for the implementation of Empowerment and Protection of Women, shall be coordinated by the Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of planning.

## Part Three

Budgeting of Programs and Activities

#### Article 26

Budgeting of programs and activities as referred to in Article 24 letter b, shall be implemented through general budget policies set forth in the Regional Revenue and Expenditure Budget.

## Part Four

Implementation of Programs and Activities

#### Article 27

Implementation of programs and activities as referred to in article 24 letter c, shall be implemented through:
a. implementation of programs and activities set forth in the budget documents of Regional Apparatus; and
b. coordination and synchronization of implementation of programs and activities with related Regional Apparatus.

## Part Five

Monitoring, Evaluation and Reporting

#### Article 28

Implementation of monitoring, evaluation and reporting as referred to in Article 24 letter d, shall be implemented through:
a. conducting monitoring and evaluation periodically of the implementation of programs and activities that have been carried out;
b. Reports shall be submitted at least 1 (one) time in 1 (one) year or at any time if necessary; and
c. evaluation results as input material for the formulation of policies, programs and activities for the following year.

# CHAPTER VIII

## INSTITUTIONAL ARRANGEMENTS

#### Article 29

1. The Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of Empowerment and Protection of Women functions as the leading sector in the implementation of Empowerment and Protection of Women.
2. Further provisions regarding the implementation of Empowerment and Protection of Women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
